# Customer messages: OData V4 service of the agents' app (benicio_1_04Srv)
#
# Start the app with `npm run cds-watch` (http://localhost:4004) and send the requests one by one
# with the VS Code extension "REST Client" or the IntelliJ HTTP client. Run them top down: the later
# requests use the message that the earlier ones create.
#
# The users are the mocked users of the development profile (the password is the user name):
# viewer reads, agent also creates and changes its own messages, admin may do everything.
# The line "# expect: <status>" documents the expected status; test/http-files.test.js sends every
# request of this directory to the application and checks it.

@host = http://localhost:4004

### Service document
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Metadata (the data model as EDMX)
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/$metadata
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### First messages with a selection of fields, sorted and counted
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages?$select=customerMessageID,customerName,productName,priorityScore,status&$orderby=customerMessageID&$top=5&$count=true
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Open messages about freezers
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages?$filter=status%20eq%20'Open'%20and%20productName%20eq%20'Freezer'&$select=customerMessageID,customerName
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Full-text search in names, IDs, texts and tags
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages?$search=warranty&$select=customerMessageID,customerName&$count=true
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Messages that carry the tag "warranty", with their tags
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages?$filter=tags/any(t:t/tag_code%20eq%20'warranty')&$select=customerMessageID&$expand=tags($expand=tag($select=title))
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### One message with its replies and tags
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=08bb27b2-9357-4598-9ea3-6b9f8dcb6d99,IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=replies($orderby=sentAt),tags($expand=tag)
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Message categories in German (Accept-Language or the URL parameter sap-locale=de select the language)
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/MessageCategories
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Accept-Language: de

### A viewer may not create a message
# expect: 403
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerMessageID": 9001
}

### Create a message: this starts a draft (the ID is chosen here so that the next requests can use it)
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
  "customerMessageID": 9001,
  "customerName": "Erika Mustermann",
  "productName": "Dishwasher",
  "customerId": "C-90001",
  "productId": "DSH-500",
  "titleCustomerLanguage": "Geschirrspüler pumpt nicht ab",
  "originatingCountry": "Germany",
  "sourceLanguage": "German",
  "fullMessageCustomerLanguage": "Nach jedem Spülgang bleibt Wasser im Geschirrspüler stehen."
}

### Change the draft
# expect: 200
PATCH {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Erika Musterfrau"
}

### Save the draft: it becomes an active message
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=false)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### The customerMessageID must be unique: this draft uses the ID of the message above...
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
  "customerMessageID": 9001
}

### ...so saving it fails with 409
# expect: 409
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002,IsActiveEntity=false)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Discard that draft
# expect: 204
DELETE {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002,IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: Basic agent agent

### Change the saved message: edit creates a new draft of it
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "PreserveChanges": true
}

### Change the new draft
# expect: 200
PATCH {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Dishwasher Pro"
}

### Save the changes
# expect: 200
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=false)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### A viewer may not delete the message (agents delete only their own messages, administrators any)
# expect: 403
DELETE {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Delete the message (the creator may)
# expect: 204
DELETE {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)
Authorization: Basic agent agent
